// Copy this file to LocalSigning.xcconfig to sign local macOS builds with your
// own Apple Development certificate. The copy is git-ignored.
//
// Signing with a stable identity stops macOS from asking for file-access,
// network, and other permissions again on every rebuild, which happens when the
// app is signed ad-hoc. Leaving this file out keeps the default ad-hoc signing
// used by CI, so do not commit your copy.
//
// Your Team ID is the OU field of your signing certificate, not the value in
// the certificate's display name. Find it with:
//
//   security find-certificate -c "Apple Development" -p \
//     | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//
// Uncomment both lines in your copy and fill in the Team ID.

// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
// CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
